{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Network AI API Request Anatomy.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Network AI API Request Anatomy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"network ai api request anatomy network ai api request anatomy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Network AI API Request Anatomy.md","fileName":"Network AI API Request Anatomy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Network AI API Request Anatomy","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI-Assisted Network Automation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI-Assisted Network Automation","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Network AI API Request Anatomy.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Network AI API Request Anatomy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"network ai api request anatomy network ai api request anatomy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Network AI API Request Anatomy.md","fileName":"Network AI API Request Anatomy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Network AI API Request Anatomy","heading":"Network AI API Request Anatomy","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A network AI API request combines an authenticated HTTP call with a selected model, an ordered message list, and generation parameters. The authorization header carries the bearer credential, the content type declares JSON, and the body distinguishes system guidance from the engineer's task.\n\nMaking the request first with a transparent client such as curl helps reveal connectivity, authentication, payload, and response failures separately. Timeouts prevent a stalled call from hanging an automation indefinitely. The returned text and finish state must be parsed and checked before any generated command or procedure enters an operational workflow.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI-A